==Trivia== 
*The word "''Archer''" comes from the Latin "''arcus"'', meaning bow. The practice of archery was first developed in Africa by the later Middle Stone Age (approx. 70,000 years ago). It is documented as part of warfare and hunting from the classical period until the late medieval period when it was made obsolete by the increased use of firearms.
**According to Clash of Clans, the bow that the Archer Queen use in [[Basics of Battle|battle]] is a modified [[X-Bow]].
**The Archer Queen is 1 of 10 [[cards]] associated with archery, with the others being [[Archers]], [[Arrows]], [[Tower Princess]], [[X-Bow]], [[Princess]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Super Archers]], and the [[Little Prince]].
*The Archer Queen is 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], Archers, [[Goblins]], [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], and [[Lava Hound]].
**She is the only troop that first existed as a Hero in Clash of Clans.
**The Archer Queen's [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Invisibility_Vial Invisibility Vial] [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Hero_Equipment equipment] in Clash of Clans functions similarly to the Cloaking Cape in Clash Royale. Unlike the Invisibility Vial, the Cloaking Cape increases the Archer Queen's attack speed instead of her damage.
*The Archer Queen is 1 of 20 cards associated with nobility, with the others being [[Knight]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Royal Giant]], [[Royal Delivery]], Tower Princess, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Prince]], [[Raging Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], Princess, [[Royal Ghost]], [[Spirit Empress]], [[Super Knight]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Royal Chef]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], and the Little Prince.
*The Archer Queen is one of the first {{Rarity|Champion}} cards to be added to the game, alongside the Golden Knight and the Skeleton King.
*Along with the Golden Knight, [[Boss Bandit]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Monk]], and the [[Terry]], the Archer Queen has the cheapest ability, costing 1 Elixir.
*The Archer Queen is 1 of 3 troops that can turn invisible and not distract other enemies, the others being [[Suspicious Bush]] and Royal Ghost.
*The Archer Queen is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], Wizard, Hog Rider, P.E.K.K.A., Dark Prince, Bowler, [[Ram Rider]], [[Electro Wizard]], Princess, [[Ice Wizard]], Magic Archer, [[Mother Witch]], [[Lumberjack]], [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], Super Magic Archer, Golden Knight, Boss Bandit, Little Prince, and the Terry.
*The Archer Queen is 1 of 3 troops that has been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt|Capture the Troop]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Treasure Hunt game mode, the others being [[Sparky]] and [[Fisherman]].
**In the Capture the Troop mode, it is possible for a player to have two {{Rarity|Champion}} cards on the field at a time. Activating the ability will activate it for both the Archer Queen and the other {{Rarity|Champion}} card.
*The Archer Queen is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being Minions, [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Tesla]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], X-Bow, Golden Knight, Skeleton King, Mighty Miner, Little Prince, and the Monk.
**It is 1 of 12 cards that is unavailable in [[Chess Royale]], the others being Royal Recruits, [[Rocket]], [[Earthquake]], [[Lightning]], [[Poison]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Miner]], Golden Knight, Skeleton King, Mighty Miner, and the Monk.
*The Archer Queen is featured in non-Clash games. More specifically: 
**The Archer Queen, along with the Goblins, Barbarians, Giant, Valkyrie, Hog Rider, Wizard, Witch, and P.E.K.K.A, were featured as a non-playable opponent in [https://www.chess.com/ Chess]. Also along with the Goblins and Golem, she was also featured as a character skin for the Queen in Chess.
**The Archer Queen is featured as [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Penny?file=Penny_Skin-Archer_Queen.png a character skin for Penny] in Brawl Stars.
**The Archer Queen, along with the P.E.K.K.A, are featured as a Hero in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*On 28 April 2022, according to a [https://twitter.com/ClashRoyale/status/1519647700085575683 tweet] by the Clash Royale official Twitter, the number of Archer Queen's ability activation was 177,904,462.
*The Archer Queen is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Archer Queen is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
